quran[20]{c,v,t}:
  26,20,"He (Moses) said: ‘I did it, but I was unaware (that a single blow would take his life)."
  26,21,"So, I fled from you, as I was afraid of you. Then, my Lord granted me divine wisdom and made me among the messengers."
  26,22,"And that blessing you are recounting to me, it was because you had enslaved the Children of Israel.’"
  26,23,Pharaoh said: ‘And what is the Lord of the worlds?’
  26,24,"He (Moses) said: ‘The Lord of all the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, if you have sure faith.’"
  26,25,He (Pharaoh) said to those around him: ‘Do you not hear?’
  26,26,He (Moses) said: ‘Your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers!’
  26,27,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Indeed your messenger, who has been sent to you, is surely crazy.’"
  26,28,"He (Moses) said: ‘The Lord of the east and the west and whatever is between them, if you can understand.’"
  26,29,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘If you take any other god besides me, I will most surely imprison you.’"
  26,30,He (Moses) said: ‘And what if I bring you something very clear?’
  26,31,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Bring it, then, if you are among the truthful.’"
  26,32,"So he (Moses) threw down his staff; behold, it was a clear serpent."
  26,33,"Then he drew out his hand (after putting it under his armpit), and behold, it was radiant white to the viewers."
  26,34,He (Pharaoh) said to the chiefs (who stood) around him: ‘This is indeed a very knowledgeable magician.
  26,35,"He wants to expel you from your land by his sorcery. So, what would you advise?’"
  26,36,They said: ‘Leave him and his brother for a while and send heralds to the cities.
  26,37,They shall bring you every expert magician.’
  26,38,So the magicians were brought together at the appointed time of a fixed day.
  26,39,And the people were told: ‘Will you gather (for this occasion)?
